  "source": "Comm-change reporting points populated from maintainer visual inspection of the printed IAA CVFR chart symbology ('נקודת מעבר קשר' — comm-transfer point legend), 2026-05-31. Call-sign frequency options are enriched from the 02/2014 Hebrew PDF table 'תדרים ואותות קריאה' plus the maintainer-provided military unit/call-sign table; assign available options per waypoint in points[].callSigns. Earlier desk-research sources (Israel eAIP 2025-10-02, PAMAT edition 1/24) did not yield OCR-extractable per-point data — see _NOTE.",
  "_definition": "Each entry marks a CVFR reporting point where pilots are expected to switch ATC frequencies because the point sits on (or at) a sector / CTR / TMA boundary. The chart annotation may be on the boundary line itself rather than directly at the point — the dataset records the *point of change*, not the chart-text position.",
  "_NOTE": "Reporting-type (חובה / דרישה — mandatory vs. on-request) is NOT comm-change and is tracked separately (PR #405). The points below come from maintainer inspection of the printed IAA CVFR chart's 'נקודת מעבר קשר' symbology, which supersedes the earlier citation bar that left this file empty. They carry verified:false because per-point frequency applicability is still being assigned. Points are matched to nav-waypoints.json by 5-letter ICAO `name` only — never by Hebrew text.",
  "_frequencySource": "תדרים ואותות קריאה, נכון לתאריך 02/2014",
  "_frequencySourceUrl": "https://sfilev1.f-static.com/image/users/262447/ftp/my_files/%D7%AA%D7%93%D7%A8%D7%99%D7%9D%20022014-2.pdf?id=14509807",
  "_militaryFrequencySource": "Maintainer-provided military unit / call-sign table, 2026-06-01",
  "_callSignsUsage": "Root callSigns is the reusable frequency catalog. Add call-sign ids to a comm-change waypoint's points[].callSigns array to expose those choices in the frequency-callout inspector. The first id becomes the default; the frequency remains editable on the note.",
